        "PMC8201384::rubric_card::000::e06b53e060"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "A thin surface oxide layer can passivate the nanoparticle surface.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "A thin protective surface oxide can form without promoting bulk phase separation.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "High configurational entropy reduces the thermodynamic driving force for segregation and phase separation at elevated temperature.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Rapid cooling kinetically limits atomic mobility.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Limiting atomic mobility prevents formation of segregated phases.",
